{
  "id": "MIC.6",
  "number": "6",
  "bookId": "MIC",
  "reference": "Micah 6",
  "verseCount": 16,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "6",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "MIC 6"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "6",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hear ye now what Jehovah saith: Arise, contend thou before the mountains, and let the hills hear thy voice. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Hear, O ye mountains, Jehovah’s controversy, and ye enduring foundations of the earth; for Jehovah hath a controversy with his people, and he will contend with Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "O my people, what have I done unto thee? and wherein have I wearied thee? testify against me. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For I brought thee up out of the land of Egypt, and redeemed thee out of the house of bondage; and I sent before thee Moses, Aaron, and Miriam. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "O my people, remember now what Balak king of Moab devised, and what Balaam the son of Beor answered him; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " from Shittim unto Gilgal, that ye may know the righteous acts of Jehovah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.5"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Wherewith shall I come before Jehovah, and bow myself before the high God? shall I come before him with burnt-offerings, with calves a year old? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "will Jehovah be pleased with thousands of rams, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " with ten thousands of rivers of oil? shall I give my first-born for my transgression, the fruit of my body for the sin of my soul? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He hath showed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth Jehovah require of thee, but to do justly, and to love kindness, and to walk humbly with thy God?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The voice of Jehovah crieth unto the city, and ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " wisdom will see thy name: hear ye the rod, and who hath appointed it. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Are there yet treasures of wickedness in the house of the wicked, and a scant measure that is abominable? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Shall I be pure with wicked balances, and with a bag of deceitful weights? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the rich men thereof are full of violence, and the inhabitants thereof have spoken lies, and their tongue is deceitful in their mouth. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Therefore I also have smitten thee with a grievous wound; I have made thee desolate because of thy sins. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt eat, but not be satisfied; and thy humiliation shall be in the midst of thee: and thou shalt put away, but shalt not save; and that which thou savest will I give up to the sword. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou shalt sow, but shalt not reap; thou shalt tread the olives, but shalt not anoint thee with oil; and the vintage, but shalt not drink the wine. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MIC 6:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the statutes of Omri are kept, and all the works of the house of Ahab, and ye walk in their counsels; that I may make thee a desolation, and the inhabitants thereof a hissing: and ye shall bear the reproach of my people.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MIC.6.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MIC.6.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
